WEBVTT

00:27.290 --> 00:29.350
So this is Marseirre.

00:32.410 --> 00:35.500
I am glad to see you look well, Master.

00:35.990 --> 00:41.310
It would appear you are performing your
duties in managing this territory admirably.

00:41.310 --> 00:42.970
Give me your report.

00:42.970 --> 00:44.580
As you wish.

00:44.580 --> 00:48.810
Here, we have the past five years of reports
on trade income and expenditures.

00:49.420 --> 00:52.100
The yearly changes in imports and exports

00:52.100 --> 00:54.780
for our top ten trading partner
nations are listed here.

00:54.780 --> 00:57.510
<i>This territory, the Archduchy of Marseirre,</i>

00:56.870 --> 01:01.710
Yes. Not bad. Both trade volume
and tax revenues are increasing.

00:57.510 --> 01:01.660
<i>is the land Her Majesty bestowed upon
Bruno for his service in treating her.</i>

01:03.290 --> 01:07.930
<i>It is a prominent trading port in the nation,
often called the gateway to the empire.</i>

01:08.430 --> 01:13.460
<i>As a major producer of medicinal herbs on top
of that, its bestowal holds great significance.</i>

01:14.430 --> 01:19.860
One issue is the Nederland East Inida
Company throwing its weight around lately.

01:20.460 --> 01:23.060
There have been cases where
it has used treaty conclusion

01:23.060 --> 01:26.100
and belligerency rights as a company
with a charter from the Nederland royals

01:26.100 --> 01:28.740
as a shield against complying with taxes.

01:29.210 --> 01:32.390
Free conduct of trade is desirable.

01:32.390 --> 01:34.700
Let's hear them out on what we can.

01:34.700 --> 01:35.970
Are you certain, my lord?

01:35.970 --> 01:39.710
Lowering tariffs improves the
flow of both goods and people.

01:40.910 --> 01:41.870
Farma.

01:43.560 --> 01:45.790
You don't need to hang around here.

01:45.790 --> 01:49.540
Master Farma, the ocean here is lovely.

01:49.760 --> 01:51.540
Th-Thanks, Father!

01:51.540 --> 01:53.860
Hurray! I'm so excited!

01:53.860 --> 01:56.150
I'm going down to the beach!

01:56.150 --> 01:58.460
Don't go into the water without an adult!

02:24.450 --> 02:30.920
<b>Parallel World Pharmacy</b>

03:39.790 --> 03:42.450
Master Farma! Come look!

03:42.450 --> 03:44.670
Brother! Look what we made!

03:45.280 --> 03:48.410
Wow. You made a castle out of sand.

03:49.510 --> 03:53.870
It's nothing compared to the
de Médicis estate, of course!

03:54.290 --> 03:57.820
Brother, can I go splash
in the water with Lotte?

03:58.080 --> 04:01.270
Father said not to go in the water.

04:01.270 --> 04:02.940
Neither of you can swim, right?

04:02.940 --> 04:04.300
Aw!

04:04.800 --> 04:08.720
Just a little, please? Pretty please?

04:13.340 --> 04:17.370
Master Farma, I'd like
to go in the water, too.

04:17.370 --> 04:19.900
I'll watch Miss Blanche.

04:21.880 --> 04:26.160
We'll stay at the water's edge
and only dip our feet in!

04:26.160 --> 04:27.540
Please? Please?

04:27.890 --> 04:29.260
Please? Please?

04:31.260 --> 04:33.980
Only your feet. Your clothes
can't touch the water.

04:33.980 --> 04:35.200
Yes, sir!

04:35.200 --> 04:36.920
Hurray!

04:38.770 --> 04:40.380
Good grief.

04:40.770 --> 04:43.840
Those two seem to be having a lot of fun.

04:44.180 --> 04:45.140
Elen.

04:49.400 --> 04:51.680
I guess I'll go take a dip, too.

04:51.680 --> 04:53.340
Do you have a change of clothes?

04:53.340 --> 04:56.190
It's fine. Nobody's watching.

05:03.610 --> 05:07.560
<i>Wait, what? </i>I'm<i> still here!</i>

05:09.810 --> 05:11.730
Farma, aren't you going to swim?

05:11.730 --> 05:13.500
Do you have a thing about the ocean?

05:13.500 --> 05:16.030
No, actually, I really lik—

05:22.520 --> 05:23.880
Go ahead. I'll stay here.

05:35.170 --> 05:39.740
<i>Come to think of it, I used to
swim in the ocean every year.</i>

05:40.310 --> 05:45.680
Bro-bro, no fair! I wanna
play in the water with you!

05:45.680 --> 05:48.150
You can when you're a little bigger.

05:48.150 --> 05:50.850
I'll get bigger right now!

05:52.080 --> 05:56.080
Beach Shack

05:57.020 --> 06:01.090
If I get bigger tomorrow, can I
play in the ocean with you then?

06:01.380 --> 06:05.330
I think it'll take longer than that.
How about next year?

06:05.330 --> 06:08.480
So, next year I can go in the water?

06:08.480 --> 06:10.800
Yup. When you're five.

06:11.080 --> 06:13.310
Okey-dokey! Next year!

06:13.310 --> 06:15.800
Pinky promise me, bro-bro!

06:17.630 --> 06:21.520
<i>Soon after, my sister's
illness was discovered.</i>

06:18.520 --> 06:24.730
<b>OPERATING ROOM</b>

06:21.520 --> 06:24.010
<i>In the end, "next year" never happened.</i>

06:35.880 --> 06:37.830
Miss Blanche!

06:42.250 --> 06:44.710
Th-The waves just...

06:44.710 --> 06:46.830
Farma, don't! I'll go after her!

06:47.660 --> 06:49.540
Blanche!

06:50.870 --> 06:53.080
The current is so fast! I can't keep up!

06:57.780 --> 06:59.080
<i>A rip current!</i>

07:01.060 --> 07:02.440
Broth—

07:07.580 --> 07:09.060
<i>Are you telling me</i>

07:09.580 --> 07:11.280
<i>I'm going to lose my little sister</i>

07:11.710 --> 07:14.130
<i>in this world, too?</i>

07:15.240 --> 07:17.720
<i>The sea currents are keeping me from her!</i>

07:17.720 --> 07:19.890
<i>If only this water were gone!</i>

07:23.830 --> 07:25.710
<i>You can't have my sister!</i>

07:25.960 --> 07:28.080
Blanche!

08:02.510 --> 08:03.880
O-Ow...

08:04.740 --> 08:06.510
What in the world just happened?

08:08.470 --> 08:09.840
Farma?!

08:24.300 --> 08:27.940
Is Farma holding the water back?

08:30.740 --> 08:31.980
<i>No...</i>

08:31.980 --> 08:35.690
<i>Even though we're on the sea floor,
the sand is dry...</i>

08:38.650 --> 08:41.350
Farma, what...

08:41.350 --> 08:43.130
What is this?

08:50.710 --> 08:54.830
Brother, I was so scared!

08:54.830 --> 08:57.540
There, there. Everything's all right now.

09:01.540 --> 09:04.820
<i>Thank goodness. She didn't inhale
or swallow much water.</i>

09:04.820 --> 09:08.230
Farma, what was that power you used?

09:09.430 --> 09:13.900
I'm not sure myself, but probably
a negative-attribute Divine Ar—

09:17.160 --> 09:20.980
Negative-attribute Arts are ultimately a
means to <i>decrease</i> the amount of a substance.

09:22.110 --> 09:27.510
You just <i>annihilated</i> it from an entire area!

09:27.510 --> 09:28.920
No such Divine Art exists!

09:36.200 --> 09:39.410
<i>What kind of mess have
I gotten myself into now?</i>

09:39.410 --> 09:42.400
Farma, you did something amazing.

09:43.320 --> 09:46.950
With my Divine Arts,
there was nothing I could do.

09:49.100 --> 09:51.860
You saved Blanche.

09:52.440 --> 09:54.020
I... saved her...

09:55.030 --> 09:57.680
Bro-bro, the beach is super fun!

09:59.440 --> 10:03.530
Brother, I'm sorry!

10:06.550 --> 10:10.800
<i>I'm so glad I could at least save you.</i>

10:18.670 --> 10:23.470
<i>At the time, I thought I had eliminated
only the seawater's water molecules...</i>

10:24.050 --> 10:26.620
<i>But there was no sign of
salt on the sea floor.</i>

10:27.150 --> 10:32.430
<i>That means I eliminated the seawater itself,
along with everything dissolved in it.</i>

10:33.340 --> 10:36.100
<i>The human body is composed
primarily of water.</i>

10:36.100 --> 10:39.720
<i>One little slip-up, and I could have
even affected Blanche and Elen...</i>

10:42.480 --> 10:47.790
<i>In the face of this strange, unknown power,
it's no wonder they'd be scared of me.</i>

10:50.490 --> 10:51.890
Master Farma.

10:52.510 --> 10:57.460
It's nearly time for bed.
Do you need anything?

10:59.360 --> 11:02.930
I'm sure you're also tired from today,
Lotte. Get plenty of rest.

11:03.300 --> 11:07.500
Yes, Master Farma. I... will see
you tomorrow morning, then.

11:17.770 --> 11:21.740
Um, Master Farma.
About what happened today...

11:22.570 --> 11:25.710
Yeah... Don't worry.
I won't do that again.

11:26.050 --> 11:26.770
Huh?

11:27.170 --> 11:29.330
Well, what I mean to say is...

11:29.860 --> 11:33.510
Try not to be too scared of me, I guess.

11:34.640 --> 11:37.560
Scared of you? Why?

11:37.560 --> 11:40.340
You seemed frightened after
you saw my Divine Art.

11:40.340 --> 11:42.050
No! I wasn't frightened!

11:42.050 --> 11:44.650
I was in awe of your Art!

11:44.650 --> 11:49.300
And the way you dove into the ocean
without hesitation was so heroic!

11:54.430 --> 11:57.150
Forgive me, Master Farma.

11:58.100 --> 12:02.060
I should have been the one
to go after your sister.

12:02.060 --> 12:03.700
I am so sorry I didn't.

12:04.820 --> 12:09.180
No, Lotte. You can't swim.
You made the right choice.

12:09.180 --> 12:11.630
I'm so glad you stayed on the shore.

12:15.800 --> 12:18.390
Blanche is my sister,
and she's important to me,

12:18.390 --> 12:22.750
but you're also important to me.
As important as family.

12:24.000 --> 12:27.230
I... don't want you to be in danger.

12:30.730 --> 12:34.240
Th-Thank you, Master Farma!
I felt trapped, and you set me free!

12:34.240 --> 12:36.180
Y-You don't need to kneel like that...

12:36.180 --> 12:41.360
I mean it! I'll remember your words
as long as I live!

12:46.540 --> 12:48.380
Good night, Master Farma.

12:57.120 --> 12:59.200
I set you free?

13:00.290 --> 13:02.700
No, you set me free.

13:16.890 --> 13:18.010
What?

13:18.010 --> 13:23.060
You're saying a kid with no shadow
completely erased seawater without a wand?

13:23.060 --> 13:28.760
Yes. Reports say a boy at an orphanage
in the Diocese of Marseirre witnessed it.

13:29.020 --> 13:31.740
A child's tall tales are of no import.

13:31.740 --> 13:33.700
Sir, several days later,

13:33.700 --> 13:37.750
a religious instructor from the
orphanage went out to the location

13:37.750 --> 13:41.040
and, upon investigation, found
abnormal Divine Power accumulations.

13:41.040 --> 13:44.750
Divine Power accumulations?
<i>Days</i> after the fact...

13:46.080 --> 13:49.250
Send instructions to every diocese
in the Saint Fleuve Empire.

13:49.250 --> 13:52.490
They are to find this child with no shadow.

13:52.490 --> 13:53.150
Yes, sir!

13:53.680 --> 13:56.440
If this report proves true,

13:56.440 --> 13:59.690
then we must eliminate this heretic.

14:07.660 --> 14:08.930
Here you go.

14:08.930 --> 14:11.870
Wow. Thanks, little lady.

14:12.160 --> 14:15.770
I know we closed for a week for
the inspection trip to Marseirre,

14:15.770 --> 14:18.100
but is it just me, or are
we busier than before?

14:18.100 --> 14:20.840
It looks like we're three times as
busy as we were before the trip.

14:20.840 --> 14:22.980
It feels like we have new customers as well.

14:23.330 --> 14:27.160
It's because you sell such good medicines.

14:27.160 --> 14:28.790
We won't be able
to close again for some time.

14:40.730 --> 14:43.910
Welcome! May I help you find something?

14:52.120 --> 14:55.690
The people in white robes seem
kinda suspicious, don't they?

14:56.100 --> 14:58.170
That was bothering me, too!

14:58.420 --> 15:01.660
If they needed to see a pharmaceutist,
they could see me.

15:01.660 --> 15:05.130
It's like they were only interested in Farma.

15:05.130 --> 15:11.140
That reminds me. I spoke to them to try
to help them, but they didn't respond.

15:11.360 --> 15:13.990
They might not be here to buy anything.

15:13.990 --> 15:17.220
They didn't seem to be looking
through the shelves.

15:17.600 --> 15:23.060
Plus, their white robes don't match the
uniforms of any guild in the city.

15:23.560 --> 15:26.640
The robes even look like
the garb of Temple priests,

15:26.640 --> 15:28.520
but they're not what I've
seen in the empire.

15:32.440 --> 15:37.400
Um, should this be brought up
with the guards?

15:37.670 --> 15:38.890
Good idea.

15:38.890 --> 15:42.720
I wouldn't want anything to happen to
the other guests, so just in case.

15:54.480 --> 15:57.160
Oh, it's shift change time already?

15:57.160 --> 15:59.020
Yes. Good job on night duty.

16:02.460 --> 16:04.520
Looks like another nice morning today.

16:19.260 --> 16:22.150
A carriage charged into the pharmacy?!

16:22.150 --> 16:24.620
I'm sorry, Master!

16:24.880 --> 16:28.720
It happened so suddenly.
There wasn't any time to stop it!

16:28.720 --> 16:31.160
Someone made a daring move...

16:31.570 --> 16:35.380
They erred in committing such
an outrage against this house.

16:35.380 --> 16:37.630
Whoever did this will pay the price!

16:37.630 --> 16:40.600
But why would someone do such a thing?

16:40.830 --> 16:42.480
To obstruct business.

16:42.480 --> 16:47.000
There are many who would resent a
newcomer selling unfamiliar medicines.

16:47.000 --> 16:49.190
I don't expect this incident
will be the last.

16:49.700 --> 16:51.960
Make haste to notify the palace.

16:52.560 --> 16:55.550
I shall make a report
to Her Majesty shortly.

16:55.550 --> 16:57.040
Y-Yes, sir!

16:58.110 --> 17:00.110
I'll go check on the pharmacy.

17:00.570 --> 17:02.630
Good. One moment, Farma.

17:02.630 --> 17:03.790
Y-Yes, Father?

17:04.120 --> 17:06.380
Do you have any suspects in mind?

17:06.810 --> 17:09.970
This is a declaration of war
against the de Médicis house.

17:10.790 --> 17:13.240
<i>It might have been the Pharmaceutist Guild,</i>

17:13.240 --> 17:16.940
<i>but those people in white robes
can't be ruled out either...</i>

17:18.770 --> 17:21.760
Overhasty action may lead to false charges.

17:22.600 --> 17:24.790
Please give me time to gather information.

17:27.730 --> 17:31.280
This foe could resort
to anything. Stay vigilant.

17:31.820 --> 17:32.700
Yes, Father.

17:41.110 --> 17:42.940
Sorry I'm late!

17:43.720 --> 17:44.900
Master Farma!

17:45.250 --> 17:48.000
What's the situation? Was anyone injured?

17:48.000 --> 17:51.880
No. But you can see the state of the store.

17:52.660 --> 17:56.080
A carriage loaded with
sediment crashed into it.

17:56.080 --> 17:59.350
The heavily damaged carriage
has been removed,

17:59.610 --> 18:01.810
but the store is still full of muck.

18:02.180 --> 18:04.260
This is awful.

18:05.480 --> 18:06.730
Purification!

18:14.350 --> 18:19.600
Given the horrid, rotten smell of this muck,
I've purified it of contaminants,

18:19.600 --> 18:21.360
but I am unable to remove the muck itself.

18:21.840 --> 18:24.350
That's plenty already. Thank you.

18:29.040 --> 18:33.400
The silver lining is that the compounding
room was completely unaffected.

18:33.400 --> 18:40.300
I had Lady Eléonore and Charlotte evacuate
to Médique with some of the medicines.

18:40.300 --> 18:42.160
Great. Thanks.

18:42.160 --> 18:44.790
If we send the prescriptions there,

18:44.790 --> 18:47.850
we can deal with the customers
who were scheduled to come in today.

18:47.850 --> 18:50.830
I'm glad. So that just leaves—

18:50.830 --> 18:53.360
Hey there, Mr. Proprietor!

18:53.360 --> 18:55.530
You're back.

18:55.530 --> 18:57.950
Today was a bit of a disaster, eh?

18:58.610 --> 18:59.960
Mr. Jean!

18:59.960 --> 19:03.000
I figured you could use help cleaning up,

19:03.000 --> 19:05.410
so I brought some of my younger men with me.

19:06.890 --> 19:11.010
They all love the Sailor's Candies you make,

19:11.010 --> 19:13.600
and they can handle heavy labor!

19:14.610 --> 19:17.350
That's a great help.
I appreciate your assistance!

19:17.640 --> 19:21.560
Now then, boys. Hop to it!

19:21.560 --> 19:23.260
You got it, boss!

19:26.880 --> 19:30.230
Sir, please don't let this get you down.

19:30.560 --> 19:33.530
I swear. Some people do awful things.

19:33.530 --> 19:36.930
If there is anything we can do
to help, please say the word.

19:36.930 --> 19:39.810
That's right! We're a community.
We help each other out!

19:39.810 --> 19:42.310
We appreciate everything you do for us!

19:50.150 --> 19:54.290
Who knew our store was already so beloved?

19:54.290 --> 19:55.630
Yeah...

19:55.970 --> 19:59.370
All of you, thank you from
the bottom of my heart!

20:01.400 --> 20:04.590
Please help! It's an emergency!

20:04.940 --> 20:07.740
Is Lord Farma the Pharmaceutist here?

20:07.740 --> 20:09.820
Please, I need your assistance!

20:10.280 --> 20:13.510
I am Farma. What is the matter?

20:13.840 --> 20:17.290
It's my father! He passed out in the heat!

20:17.690 --> 20:21.300
It's already been so long,
but he isn't waking up!

20:21.840 --> 20:23.310
I understand.

20:25.360 --> 20:27.780
We've got this. Go on.

20:27.780 --> 20:29.910
Leave the cleanup to us!

20:30.910 --> 20:32.040
That's right!

20:32.040 --> 20:33.230
We'll see you later!

20:33.230 --> 20:34.570
Don't worry about things here!

20:34.880 --> 20:37.590
I can handle things here.

20:38.850 --> 20:40.100
Thanks.

20:40.890 --> 20:42.980
Then I have a patient to see.

20:51.440 --> 20:55.520
Lord Farma, this way. My father is up ahead.

20:55.520 --> 20:56.100
Got it.

20:56.620 --> 20:58.880
<i>Dehydration or heat stroke...</i>

20:58.880 --> 21:00.800
<i>Cerebrovascular disease
or a convulsion...</i>

21:00.800 --> 21:02.550
<i>Or possibly, physical trauma, too.</i>

21:03.440 --> 21:06.980
<i>I brought some first aid supplies,
just in case.</i>

21:08.140 --> 21:11.510
Oh, Lord Farma, just over that hill.

21:11.940 --> 21:12.920
This way!

21:20.590 --> 21:25.340
<i>This is a fairly remote area.
We're quite a ways from the city.</i>

21:26.180 --> 21:28.310
Miss, where is your father?

21:29.290 --> 21:30.230
Huh?

21:38.940 --> 21:40.050
<i>Oh, no!</i>

21:48.030 --> 21:50.990
You're the one who erased
the sea in Marseirre.

21:50.990 --> 21:53.050
The boy with no shadow. Correct?

21:55.200 --> 21:56.370
Answer.

21:57.200 --> 22:02.290
We are inquisitors from the Holy Kingdom.

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Episode 7</b>
